text-align in CSS

The CSS text-align property is used to align text horizontally inside an element.
Syntax
selector {
    text-align: value;
}

| Value     | Meaning                                       |
| --------- | --------------------------------------------- |
| `left`    | Aligns text to the left                       |
| `center`  | Aligns text to the center                     |
| `right`   | Aligns text to the right                      |
| `start`   | Aligns according to the writing direction     |
| `end`     | Aligns opposite to `start`                    |


