<section> in HTML

The <section> element is a semantic HTML5 element used to group related content together.

Syntax
<section>
    <h2>Section Title</h2>
    <p>Section content goes here.</p>
</section>

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
<footer> in HTML
The <footer> element is a semantic HTML5 element used to define the footer (bottom section) of a webpage or a section.

Basic Syntax :
<footer>
    Footer content
</footer>

Easy way to remember:
<footer> = Bottom/closing information of a webpage or section, such as copyright, contact information, navigation links, and social-media links.

<section> vs <div>
| `<section>`                                | `<div>`                        |
| ------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------ |
| Semantic element                           | Non-semantic element           |
| Represents a meaningful section of content | Generic container              |
| Usually has a heading                      | Heading is not required        |
| Helps SEO and accessibility                | Mainly used for styling/layout |

