box-shadow in CSS

The box-shadow property is used to add a shadow around an HTML element, such as a <div>, card, button, or image.

Syntax
box-shadow: horizontal vertical blur spread color;

Example :
.box {
    width: 200px;
    height: 100px;
    background-color: white;

    box-shadow: 5px 5px 10px gray;
}

Understanding the Values :

box-shadow: 5px 5px 10px gray;
            │    │    │    │
            │    │    │    └── Color
            │    │    └─────── Blur
            │    └──────────── Vertical
            └───────────────── Horizontal

